From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Kulinich <entaytion@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:13:29 +0300
Subject: fix(translate): fix stock-side translation hooks

Stock-Java half of an audit-driven cleanup of the third-party translate
integration; the Kotlin-side fixes for the same audit live in the main
git repo (src/kotlin), not in this patch stack.

- drop 3 dead language-filter call sites (TranslateButton/TranslateAlert3/
  AIEditorAlert) now that no provider restricts target languages; the
  Kotlin-side machinery they called into was removed in the same cleanup
- getDialogTranslateTo: drop an unreachable null check and route through
  TranslateHelper.currentTargetLanguage() instead of a 4th duplicate of
  the same "target language or fallback" logic
- invalidateTranslation: also clear the fork's own shadow state (webPages/
  bodies/manual) when stock invalidates a translation, so a stale
  translated link preview no longer outlives the message it belonged to
- pushToTranslate: reorder error branches so TO_LANG_INVALID/QUOTA_EXCEEDED
  are checked before the generic non-transcription fallback, which had
  started swallowing every error before those two could ever fire
- checkTranslation (whole-chat auto-translate): record the same
  pre-translation baseline and "keep original" merged body the manual
  translate path already builds, so KEEP_ORIGINAL_AFTER_TRANSLATION and
  edit-invalidation protection now also cover auto-translated dialogs,
  not just messages translated via the manual long-press menu
